# Sapio MCP Server - Cursor Rules for Code Compliance

## ⚠️ MANDATORY FIRST STEP - READ BEFORE PROCEEDING ⚠️

**🚨 CRITICAL: You MUST complete this step before generating ANY Sapio code:**

### Pre-Flight Checklist:
- [ ] Step 1: Read the full Sapio coding standards (all sections). In **Cursor**, read **`.cursorrules`** in this repo (or use **`.cursor/rules/sapio-compliance.mdc`** when that rule is installed); with the **Sapio MCP server**, fetch **`sapio://docs/cursor-rules`** (same standards).
- [ ] Step 2: Output the following acknowledgment statement verbatim BEFORE any code generation:
  ```
  "I have read Sapio's .cursorrules file for best practices and coding standards."
  ```
- [ ] Step 3: Before acting or planning, review the MCP server: call list_sapio_resources() and fetch sapio://meta/tool-index. For **Java** plugins, fetch sapio://preprompts/java. For **Python** webhooks or sapiopy work, fetch sapio://preprompts/python and sapio://examples/python/... (use get_sapio_python_webhook_prompt() as a shortcut). When the Sapio MCP server is available, use these resources before generating code—not only local files or site-packages.
- [ ] Step 4: Only after completing the steps above, proceed with code generation

**Failure to output the acknowledgment statement will result in non-compliant code that violates project standards.**

### Why This Matters:
- Ensures awareness of modern package patterns (`com.velox.sapio.commons`)
- Prevents use of deprecated APIs
- Enforces batch operations and performance best practices
- Maintains consistency across all Sapio code generation

---

## Project Overview
This is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for Sapio LIMS/ELN extension patterns: **Java server plugins** and **Python webhooks** (same server). It provides examples and pre-prompts for both; the MCP server is **not Java-only**.

## Rule Acknowledgment (Required)
**Before generating any Sapio code, you MUST output the following statement:**
"I have read Sapio's .cursorrules file for best practices and coding standards."

This confirms you are aware of and will follow all guidelines in this file.

---

## Using MCP Server Tools for Code Generation

When the Sapio MCP server is available:
- **Before acting or planning on a task**, call list_sapio_resources() and fetch sapio://meta/tool-index. For **Java** plugins, fetch sapio://preprompts/java (Plugin/scenario → Resource table). For **Python** webhooks, CallbackUtil, CommonsWebhookHandler, or REST from webhooks, fetch sapio://preprompts/python and the matching sapio://examples/python/... resources (tool get_sapio_python_webhook_prompt() summarizes URIs).
- **Before generating any Sapio code**, fetch resource sapio://docs/cursor-rules and adhere to the returned rules (Java and Python sections as applicable).
- **For workflow and resource mapping**, use the preprompt for your stack (java vs python); when unsure, fetch sapio://meta/tool-index first (or list_sapio_resources() then fetch the relevant sapio:// URI).

**If the MCP server is unreachable, I must inform the user.**

